 "captions": {
  "script": "These neon pools look alive. But nothing can live in them. Glitch Diary, entry eleven. Dallol, in Ethiopia's Danakil Depression. It sits more than a hundred meters below sea level. In the nineteen-sixties, a camp here averaged about thirty-five degrees Celsius. All year round. A record for any place people have lived. But that's not the strange part. The pools are hot and salty. And so acidic, their pH drops below zero. Those yellows and greens? Not algae. Just iron and salt minerals. And scientists still can't agree on one thing... In twenty nineteen, one team reported tiny microbes here. Another team searched the pools and found no life at all. Only crystals that look like cells. Would you dare walk here? Tell me in the comments. Follow for the next entry of my glitch diary. Because these pools only look alive...",
